  "reason": "Evidence: config_016 (multimodal, singleprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, concat) achieved 0.527 acc, a meaningful +4.2pt gain over RNA-only (config_001, 0.485), confirming that the image modality contributes positively. However, we have no information on whether multiprofile aggregation (avgpool/transformer) can further improve performance beyond singleprofile. Question: config_018 extends config_016 by switching to multiprofile with avgpool aggregation while keeping the same RNA encoder (pca_n2000), image encoder (resnet50), and fusion (concat), isolating the effect of multi-profile aggregation. Why this is the best next experiment: With 7 experiments remaining, resolving whether multiprofile helps is the highest-leverage design question because it determines whether the remaining budget should explore the multiprofile branch (configs 018-027, 030-051) or focus on singleprofile variants (fusion, encoder swaps). If multiprofile+avgpool improves on 0.527, we can then test transformer aggregation and weighted fusion as logical extensions. If it does not, we avoid wasting experiments on that branch and pivot to fusion/encoder comparisons within singleprofile."
}

